      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You've identified a critical ethical challenge; neighborhood metrics like tenure can act as unfair proxies for protected classes and historical redlining patterns if not carefully vetted. To prevent this, you should conduct extensive subgroup analyses to detect adverse impacts and intentionally debias the weights of these features or replace them with more granular, individual-focused data points. It is often wiser to terminate non-traditional neighborhood features entirely or use a constrained data subset that strictly excludes geocoded demographic variables to avoid embedding systemic bias directly into your scoring engine.",
      "source": "target",
